WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.602
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers,
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.803
We hope you're all
doing well tonight.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.471
I'm in a stranger's apartment.

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.039
Let's get to the news.

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:09.108
During a speech yesterday
in Atlanta,

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:11.978
President Biden endorsed
changing the Senate filibuster

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:15.081
in order to pass federal
voting rights legislation

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.684
and said, "I'm tired
of being quiet."

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.952
Quiet?

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:21.754
When did we ever say
we wanted a quiet president?

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:24.190
Oh, right. Okay, yeah.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.526
Yeah, we may have
put it out there.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:29.729
During a hearing yesterday,
Republican Senator Richard Burr

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.531
criticized the
Biden Administration's

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.299
Coronavirus pandemic messaging

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:36.769
and said that the American
people are "confused."

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:38.203
Said Biden, "It's simple.

00:00:38.203 --> 00:00:40.039
Just wear a mask indoors.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:41.708
Unless you're indoors,
and then you can

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.142
safely make outdoors indoors

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:45.411
so long as your booster stays
six feet away

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:46.579
from sheltering in place."

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:49.048
Come on, Jack!

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:50.550
A new op-ed
in "The Wall Street Journal"

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.852
suggests that Hillary Clinton
could be the best

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.721
Democratic nominee for the 2024
presidential election,

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.824
because all voters
really want right now

00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:00.927
is someone who admits it
when they lose.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:03.263
The House committee
investigating the Capitol attack

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:07.032
has subpoenaed two advisers
to Donald Trump Jr.

00:01:07.032 --> 00:01:13.038
to try to find out
what exactly it is that they do.

00:01:13.038 --> 00:01:14.674
Former President Trump
reportedly hung up

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:17.510
on NPR journalist
Steve Inskeep yesterday

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.946
just 9 minutes
into a 15-minute interview.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:21.848
Though, to be fair, who among us

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:26.686
hasn't tapped out 9 minutes
into a 15-minute NPR segment?

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:29.022
I say that as a fan.

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.823
Been there.

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.492
Former Democratic presidential
hopefuls Andrew Yang

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:35.528
and Marianne Williamson
had dinner on Monday

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:36.762
in New York City.

00:01:36.762 --> 00:01:40.266
"Please, no photos,"
said the restaurant.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:43.703
Kellogg's recently released
a Valentine's Day-themed

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:49.476
Froot Loops cereal that
includes heart-shaped pieces.

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:51.244
But if that's
what she wants this year,

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:53.513
she's too young for you, dude!

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:57.450
Does it look like
I'm looking at him?

00:01:58.517 --> 00:02:00.153
Listen, you guys know,
in reality,

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:02.622
I'm just looking at a wall.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:06.726
Amazon founder Jeff Bezos
turned 58 years old today.

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:09.161
If you want to wish him a happy
birthday, just say it out loud.

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:13.132
I'm sure one of your devices
will get the message to him.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:16.035
Pope Francis visited
a record shop in Rome yesterday

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.369
and left with a CD.

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:19.471
And I gotta say,
I didn't even realize

00:02:19.471 --> 00:02:22.674
the Popemobile had visors.

00:02:22.674 --> 00:02:26.212
Two of our writers
wrote that joke.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:27.814
Which is weird,
because all of our writers

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:30.683
are 22 or younger.

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.420
And, finally... [ Laughs ]

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.289
And finally, the Girl Scouts
have partnered with

00:02:37.289 --> 00:02:40.793
the delivery platform DoorDash
to allow local troops

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.695
to sell cookies through the app.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.263
Meanwhile, at the Boy Scouts?

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:47.533
Still trying to make a fire
with sticks.

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:50.803
They develop slower.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.638
It's just a boy/girl thing.

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:53.940
You guys, that was
the monologue.

